    <tags>audio sound default-device playback recording headset tray windows utility</tags>

    <summary>Stops Windows from switching your audio device every time you plug something in.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
Windows changes your default playback, recording and communications devices on
its own, whenever a headset, a monitor or a dock appears or disappears. If you
have ever finished a call and found your game audio coming out of the monitor
speakers, that is this.

AudioWinFix pins the devices you chose. Plug and unplug all you like: what you
picked stays picked. Switching by hand still works and is taken as the new
intent, so it stays out of the way rather than fighting you.

It sits in the tray, uses no perceptible resources, and needs no configuration
beyond telling it once what you want.

**About this package**

Installs the portable build, machine-wide, and updates through Chocolatey. The
installer on the releases page instead installs per user and updates itself; use
whichever suits how you manage the machine.
]]></description>

    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/Kenshin9977/AudioWinFix/releases/tag/v$version$</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>

  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
